# Watch policies (FAZA 3, defect D-A) -- META-REPO's own set.
#
# FORMAT, one policy per line:
#     <policy-name> -- <glob>[, <glob>...]
# Names are lowercase [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*. '#' comments and blanks are
# ignored. Pathspec magic (a line or glob starting ':', '-', '!') is
# REFUSED: these are CLI globs handed to match_paths(), never git
# pathspecs (SI-1, same rule as .truth/citation-scope).
#
# Use:  scripts/truth claim "..." --watch-policy fold-kernel ...
# The policy RESOLVES to the watch set; --paths and --watch-policy cannot
# be combined. The resolved globs are still stored on the claim, so a
# later edit here never rewrites what a past claim is understood to have
# watched -- the ledger is append-only and the name is provenance.
#
# NOT YAML on purpose: the CLI is stdlib-only (scripts/truth line 20), so
# a .yml extension would promise a generality the loader has to refuse.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS -- the measurement, 2026-08-17:
#   75 active claims carry a watch set.
#   Those 75 sets are 60 DISTINCT sets.
# Reuse is essentially zero: nearly every claim re-invented its watch set
# freehand, and nothing checked the set against the evidence. J-022 found
# five claims drifted in BOTH directions at once -- watching an ADR file
# their recipe never opens, while missing a suite file it does open.
#
# The surviving cost of that is ATTENTION, not false stalings: since the
# step-2.5 double-invalidation rule a path touch stales nothing, but the
# whisper still fires on every watched path. Measured over the last 200
# commits: 1670 whisper lines, a mean of 22.6 claims named per edit.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-18 (J-040 recounted; the correction had never reached
# this file). The first pass summed per FILE and reported 2329 lines /
# 6.8 claims per edit, but the whisper emits ONE line per CLAIM: both
# terms were inflated and the ratio came out over three times too low.
# The conclusion is unchanged and stronger, which is why nothing below
# was re-argued.
#
# The policies below are NOT invented. Each is a watch set that recurring
# claims already share, named after the SURFACE its evidence reads. Step
# 3.3 migrates the existing claims onto them.

# --- test surfaces -------------------------------------------------------
canary-suite -- template/scripts/truth-canary.sh
core-suite -- template/scripts/test-truth-core.py
both-suites -- template/scripts/test-truth-core.py, template/scripts/truth-canary.sh

# --- CLI behaviour -------------------------------------------------------
# A behaviour claim reads the code that implements it AND the seeded-fault
# arm that pins it; that pairing is the most common set in the ledger.
cli-behaviour -- template/truthlib/cli.py, template/scripts/truth-canary.sh
fold-kernel -- template/truthlib/kernel.py, template/scripts/truth-canary.sh
record-contract -- template/.truth/schema/claims.schema.json, template/truthlib/kernel.py, template/scripts/truth-canary.sh
truthlib-package -- template/truthlib/**

# --- meta-repo surfaces (untemplated: these paths exist only here) -------
release-battery -- scripts/release-battery.sh
paper -- docs/truth-ledger-paper-v3.md
